From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 09:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vxlan: remove the wire actually found, and treat not-found as
 success

0013 taught CreateOrUpdate to SEE a KubeVirt bridge-binding-renamed wire
("podXXXX" renamed to "XXXX-nic", enslaved to "k6t-XXXX") by looking up the
renamed form and setting `link = renamed`. It left veth.LinkName as the
ORIGINAL "podXXXX". That is fine while the found wire's attrs match; the
moment they differ (a peer whose VTEP moved, or a wire left behind by an
earlier incarnation of the peer) the attrs-differ branch calls
veth.RemoveVethLink(), koko does LinkByName("podXXXX") INSIDE the netns, the
name no longer exists there, and the daemon returns it as fatal:

  failed to lookup "pod980816f36b7" in "/var/run/netns/cni-...": Link not found

The CNI ADD fails, kubelet recreates the sandbox, and because the VNI is
deterministic per link (0006) every retry recomputes the same request and
hits the same wall FOREVER. The else-branch removal for a found non-vxlan
link carried the same latent defect.

Measured 2026-09-05 (Loki, meshnet daemon on worker-a): example-lab pod
virt-launcher-siteB-cor-sw01 on sm-node-b, 776+ sandbox recreations at ~2s
intervals, restarts=0, every retry failing on that exact line; the dangling
wire lives in the PEER pod siteB-fw01's netns on worker-a. This is the sibling
sub-case 0013 did not cover: 0013 made the renamed wire visible, but never
made it REMOVABLE.

Both call sites now go through removeExistingWire, which (1) removes the
link under the name it was actually FOUND as -- the name the kernel knows --
and (2) treats a not-found result as success with an Info log, because the
postcondition of "remove the old wire" already holds when the wire is
absent. Every other removal error is still returned under the two existing
MESHNETD error strings. koko formats the lookup failure with %v, which
breaks the error chain, so the substring "Link not found" is the match that
fires in production; errors.As on netlink.LinkNotFoundError is kept for a
koko that wraps with %w.

The remover is injected so daemon/vxlan/vxlan_remove_test.go proves both
rules without a netns. The tests are a positive control: against the pre-fix
body (name untouched, every error fatal) TargetsTheLinkActuallyFound and
TreatsNotFoundAsSuccess go RED and the rest stay green -- run and observed
2026-09-05 with a byte-copied swap of the helper body.

---
 daemon/vxlan/vxlan.go             |  82 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 daemon/vxlan/vxlan_remove_test.go | 161 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 241 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 daemon/vxlan/vxlan_remove_test.go

--- a/daemon/vxlan/vxlan.go
+++ b/daemon/vxlan/vxlan.go
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
